[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4384174457","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119164#issuecomment-4384174457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119164","id":4384174457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBVExeQ","user":{"login":"vaner-org","id":9658355,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk2NTgzNTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9658355?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org","html_url":"https://github.com/vaner-org","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vaner-org/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T00:20:43Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T00:53:20Z","body":"This is not a bug, nor something that needs to happen, as it would only affect the AnimationNodeAnimation type, and lead to a host of complications. The blend point name is a string that is user-editable, and is detached from its contents after creation, see StateMachine for similar behaviour. It may also be incremented for duplicates: one, one 2, one 3. You may however edit the name of the blend point to be anything by clicking on it, same as StateMachine.\n\nSo, instead of this:\n\n> The current workaround seems to require deleting the point and adding it with the expected animation name.\n\nMaybe a better approach would be to click the label, clear the name, and a new one would be chosen corresponding to the current animation. That was part of #110369's original design, but was changed to entirely reject empty names. That could be a good enhancement for both StateMachine and BlendSpaces, but unfortunately would only be useful for AnimationNodeAnimation.\n\nThe main problem here seems to be that the inline editing of the blend point name needs documentation, and an intimation in the 4.7 release announcement.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4384174457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4384425073","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119164#issuecomment-4384425073","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119164","id":4384425073,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBVUEcQ","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T01:24:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T01:24:10Z","body":"So we should add something like `click to sync the node name of AnimationNodeAnimation`?\nBut, it also only aimed to `AnimationNodeAnimation`. I cannot tell the different between updating node name automaticly and by hand.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4384425073/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451062935","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119164#issuecomment-4451062935","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119164","id":4451062935,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCU3Ulw","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-14T13:27:28Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T13:28:31Z","body":"This is not a bug. As I mentioned in the comment in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119246#pullrequestreview-4290259916.\n\n> The blend point names in AnimationBlendSpace are managed separately from the assigned Animation.\n\n> To give a similar example, changing the animation assigned to an AnimationNodeAnimation placed within an AnimationNodeBlendTree does not change the name of the AnimationNode.\n\n> Also, you can place multiple instances of the same Animation within a BlendSpace, and they must have different names.\nChanging the point name when the assigned Animation resource is changed is clearly the wrong approach.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4451062935/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]